 "スッと": "مُسْتَقِيم (Not crooked, curly, or bent; having a constant direction throughout its length.) / عَلَى طُول (Of a direction relative to the subject, precisely; as if following a direct line)  [straight]\nスーッと and すうっと are more emphatic\nمثال: 彼はそのそばでシャツをすうっと着た。\n→ He slipped the gaudy shirt on. / بِهُدُوء (Producing little or no noise.)  [quietly] / [to feel refreshed ; to feel satisfied]",
 "スッカラカン": "[completely empty]\nمثال: うるさいなっ！少しの頭痛くらい我慢しろ。余は魔力がすっからかんだ。それもこれも姫のせいだぞ。\n→ Shurrup! Don't make such a fuss over a little headache. I'm flat out of magical power - this is all your fault! / فقير (utterly without money)  [penniless]\nمثال: 今週末は温泉に行く余裕はないね。すっからかんだ。\n→ I can't afford to go to the onsen this weekend. I'm broke.",
